WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.150
Low prices!

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:04.230
Snacks are a bargain today!

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.270
These popular snacks are half-priced!

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:14.700
Crispy Lollypops and soy sauce-flavored
Fluffy Chocolate Octopus Dumplings.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.950
They’re real, but they’re half-priced.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.110
Everyone, be careful!

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:23.130
Something’s fishy about these snacks!

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:23.820
Fishy?

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:25.110
There’s something fishy?

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:29.380
Kid, you have a problem
with my store?

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:32.260
I only told the truth.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:34.180
The world is full of secrets.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.970
I’ll prove that in a duel.

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:39.840
Here I go!

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:43.640
I activate
the Continuous Trap Ultra C!

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:45.310
What’s that card?

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:48.190
I Special Summon Grenosaurus!

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:00.740
Understand?

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:03.230
This is life!

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:07.320
As promised, I’ll take this.

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:10.750
There’s always something behind everything.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:13.760
Why snacks have a half-off sale.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:15.720
Why mom is happy.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:17.990
Why there’s no homework.

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:22.900
I’m telling you, it’s true—

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.580
Upside-down?

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:27.650
It was him!

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:31.770
There’s always something behind everything.

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:33.220
Cleaning. Cleaning.

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:36.110
Even he’s hiding something.

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:38.200
Upside-down.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.910
The most suspicious
person right now... is him!

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:44.240
Yuma Tsukumo.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:48.140
I forgot that my sister
asked me to go shopping!

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:53.920
That boy...

00:01:53.920 --> 00:02:00.510
Yuma Tsukumo is bad at dueling, but he defeated
Shark who competed in the national tournament.

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:03.480
There’s definitely something behind this.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:05.980
He must have a powerful card.

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:12.080
To get that card, I’ll give him this card and make him duel.

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:19.530
Astral?

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:22.550
That’s what he wants
you to call him.

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:24.620
Who?

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:27.580
You always call him a ghost.

00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:33.340
He says, “My name isn’t Ghost.
I’m Astral from Astral World.”

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:35.950
He’s here.

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:40.180
This guy kept bothering me
about it since yesterday.

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:42.930
My name isn’t “This Guy.”
It’s Astral.

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:44.740
I know!

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:46.400
He named him.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.000
He’s mentally ill.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.390
Yuma!

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:51.580
It’s Yuma!

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:53.110
Tokunosuke.

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:55.970
What were you talking about?

00:02:55.970 --> 00:02:58.610
Were you badmouthing me?

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:01.980
But I don’t care.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:04.700
It’s okay to badmouth me.
Gossiping is great!

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:08.450
If I remember correctly,
I saw him yesterday.

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:09.790
Who are you?

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:11.690
You don’t know who I am?

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:13.970
On the surface,
I’m a regular middle school student.

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:16.380
But secretly, I’m also
a regular middle school student.

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:19.380
I’m the same both
front and back!

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:22.130
I’m Tokunosuke Omoteura!

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:25.920
I’m in the class next door.

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:29.810
I wanted to give
you this, Yuma.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:33.560
It’s an Xyz Monster, Baby Tiragon!

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:35.770
Xyz Monster?

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:38.530
It’s thanks for defeating Shark!

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:41.980
He did a lot
of horrible things to me.

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:44.240
It’s a symbol of our friendship!

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:46.200
A symbol of friendship.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:49.700
I can really have it?

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:54.480
What’s that strange thing
flowing out of his body?

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:58.090
Don’t be modest. Take it.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:00.840
In that case, I’ll take it.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:01.800
Yuma!

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:04.140
You’re watering the flowers today!

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:08.240
Hurry up or you
won’t finish in time.

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:10.970
But the card!

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:14.750
You can’t take Tokunosuke’s card.

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:17.480
Why not?

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:20.850
We know because we’ve had the same class
with him since elementary school.

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:23.620
There’s always something behind his actions.

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:24.660
Be careful.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:25.600
Behind?

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:27.370
What are you talking about?

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:29.350
He doesn’t seem like that.

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:32.620
They’re in my way.

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:35.540
But I’m not giving up.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:38.420
I will give him this card.

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:45.760
Whether it’s rain, wind,
blizzard or the scorching sun

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:48.530
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:51.470
Your kindness was harsh I learned frustration when we clashed

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:55.660
Freedom begins by accepting differences
Dance and create the universe

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:03.440
In truth, I was sad
until I met you

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:09.730
I lied, thinking it was
easier to be alone

00:05:09.730 --> 00:05:16.130
Even though we don’t like
the same books or hobbies

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:20.020
You’re the only one
who agreed with me

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:22.840
Joy and sadness and anger
and do re mi fa so la ti do

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:25.160
There’s no harmony and scenario
without differences

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:28.550
Everyone is not the same

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:33.220
That’s the reason for living

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:38.900
Even if the sounds
are dissonant at times

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:43.930
That’s why I never give up!
I believe my strength will get me through

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:47.570
I travel to
the edge of the world

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:52.030
The sights I see
with you are the truth

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:54.870
Whether it’s rain, wind,
blizzard or the scorching sun

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:58.120
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:01.420
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:05.170
Freedom begins by accepting differences
Dance and create the universe

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:14.720
So in this case,
the correct answer is...

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:19.230
Outwit the Duel!

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:19.230
Number 5:

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:19.230
Outwit the Duel!

00:06:16.210 --> 00:06:20.830
This gigantic structure is divided into many blocks.

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:22.560
Why?

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:25.880
Anyway, that boy...

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.250
What’s this?

00:06:57.790 --> 00:06:59.670
Yuma!

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:04.130
Yuma!

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:06.120
The card!

00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:08.570
Hey!

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:10.020
Yuma!

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:14.860
You always have your guard down!

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:17.250
Aren’t you too suspicious?

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:20.920
They’re completely guarding him!

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:24.150
At this rate, I can’t
give Yuma this card.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:28.380
I wonder if anyone dropped
an Xyz Monster.

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:31.630
That’s Taichi, Yuma’s classmate.

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:33.780
I can use him.

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:36.350
What? Really?

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:38.090
I promise.

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:40.480
I’ll definitely go!

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:43.060
Hooray! I’m so lucky!

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:45.490
Everything is useful when used correctly.

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:47.570
The first stage is complete.

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:48.850
I’m home!

00:07:48.850 --> 00:07:49.490
Yuma!

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:53.360
You’re not playing
Duel Monsters, are you?

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:54.990
Of course not.

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:56.820
Then what’s this?

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:01.980
To the duel king Yuma.

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:03.830
From Yuma’s biggest fan.

00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:06.290
No way! Fan mail?

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:09.100
Oh oh!

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:11.100
Yuma!

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:14.720
I keep telling him
that he’s not allowed to duel.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:17.130
Grandma, did you know about this?

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:23.230
For Yuma, duels aren’t just duels.

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:25.960
Where were you?

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:27.230
Whatever.

00:08:28.280 --> 00:08:32.010
Isn’t this awesome? It’s fan mail!

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:37.700
Aren’t you going to ask me,
“What kind of effect is fan mail?”

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:42.870
Fan mail is a letter that says you’re
a big fan who loves me!

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:46.580
Yuma, you’re not allowed to duel?

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:49.540
That’s none of your business.

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:52.050
Anyway, my fan mail!

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:56.760
Observation #8:
Yuma is not allowed to duel.

00:08:58.810 --> 00:09:03.940
This is the Baby Tiragon card
that Tokunosuke tried to give me.

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:13.910
I saved my allowance
to buy it. Please use it.

00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:18.030
What a coincidence!

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:22.580
Hooray! It’s an Xyz Monster!

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:25.480
The second stage is complete.

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:27.850
All that’s left is
the finishing touch.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:33.850
I’ll paste this on that...

00:09:33.850 --> 00:09:36.630
Now Yuma is finished.

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:39.650
You’ll learn
that life can be cruel.

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:43.500
Good morning!

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:44.680
Yuma!

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:49.940
I never thought you would do
such things behind-the-scenes!

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:52.400
Behind-the-scenes? Did I do something?

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:56.070
“Do something?” How shameless!

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:59.870
Anonymous photos were sent
to everyone’s cell phones!

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:02.740
To summarize,
we know what you did!

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:04.200
You wrecked the flowers!

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:06.120
You pulled a prank
on the teacher!

00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:08.370
You cheated during the test!

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:12.710
And you ate Taichi’s lunch
and replaced it with a frog!

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:16.170
Taichi was hurt,
so he’s absent today!

00:10:17.390 --> 00:10:19.230
Taichi?

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:22.140
There’s no way
I would do this!

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:24.100
That’s what I keep saying!

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:26.100
This is a mistake!

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:29.520
Yuma doesn’t do things behind-the-scenes!

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:36.240
I know you want to protect Yuma,
but there’s proof.

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:39.720
Yuma, I’m no longer your friend.

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:41.580
Everyone, let’s go.

00:10:42.630 --> 00:10:44.340
Wait a second!

00:10:44.340 --> 00:10:48.320
If you deal with Yuma,
nothing good happens.

00:10:49.270 --> 00:10:51.540
It wasn’t me!

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:54.300
The plan is a great success.

00:11:01.670 --> 00:11:03.850
There’s no one
to duel here either.

00:11:05.320 --> 00:11:08.010
Why did this happen?

00:11:08.010 --> 00:11:09.600
I didn’t do anything.

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:12.310
What kind of effect is “behind?”

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:13.940
Behind?

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:18.120
That effect is the reason
why everyone hates you.

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:23.620
Behind means that you say something different
than what you actually believe.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:25.630
Something different?

00:11:25.630 --> 00:11:28.470
Is that a human characteristic?

00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:30.290
All humans have it.

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:33.250
Then why don’t you have it?

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:36.960
I do too!

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:38.920
Yuma!

00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:41.680
What are you doing here?

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:43.260
Tokunosuke?

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:50.840
So that’s what happened.

00:11:50.840 --> 00:11:54.480
They totally ignore me,
so I feel sad.

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:57.570
I believe you, Yuma.

00:11:57.570 --> 00:12:01.490
I saw your duel with Shark.

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:03.530
I know the truth
because I watched you duel.

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:06.080
Tokunosuke...

00:12:07.730 --> 00:12:12.180
By the way, what was that card
you used to defeat Shark?

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:14.180
You mean Utopia?

00:12:14.180 --> 00:12:16.950
Oh yeah, that’s right!

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:20.530
Utopia...

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:24.480
His strange power is getting stronger.

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:26.260
What’s going on?

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:31.740
Cheer up. No matter what
anyone says, I have your back.

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:34.940
What was that?

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:39.640
Tokunosuke, you’re a really good guy.

00:12:40.310 --> 00:12:42.650
Anyway, do you want to duel?

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:43.490
Duel?

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:46.210
This is the best
time to duel.

00:12:46.210 --> 00:12:47.990
A duel will make
you feel better.

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:50.700
All right! Let’s duel!

00:12:51.390 --> 00:12:53.380
The idiot fell for it.

00:12:53.380 --> 00:12:56.460
Now Utopia is mine.

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:59.050
You shouldn’t duel him.

00:12:59.050 --> 00:13:00.480
I have a bad feeling.

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:01.880
A bad feeling?

00:13:02.530 --> 00:13:05.940
Even you’re accusing Tokunosuke?

00:13:05.940 --> 00:13:09.040
Tokunosuke is trying
to cheer me up!

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:11.570
That’s what friendship is!

00:13:11.570 --> 00:13:13.850
Why are you talking to yourself?

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:15.700
It’s nothing.

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:17.860
Let’s hurry up and duel!

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:21.030
Here I go! I’m kattobing!

00:13:21.540 --> 00:13:23.690
D-Gazer set!

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:26.280
Target locked on!

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:30.910
AR Vision Link complete.

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:35.290
Duel!

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:39.670
I’ll go first!

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:42.210
My turn! I draw!

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:45.480
I set a monster
in face-down defense position!

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:47.890
I end my turn!

00:13:47.890 --> 00:13:50.510
You’re strengthening your defense!

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:53.250
Yuma, you defeated Shark.

00:13:53.250 --> 00:13:55.210
I have to proceed carefully.

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:59.790
Yuma, you should also proceed
in this duel carefully.

00:13:59.790 --> 00:14:02.110
Be quiet! Shut up!

00:14:02.640 --> 00:14:05.020
He’s talking to himself again.

00:14:05.020 --> 00:14:06.820
Is this some kind of strategy?

00:14:07.270 --> 00:14:11.590
For a face-down defense position monster,
I don’t know its DEF unless I attack it.

00:14:11.590 --> 00:14:21.610
But if I attack carelessly and its DEF are greater
than my ATK, I’ll take the difference as damage.

00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:22.880
In that case...

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:25.540
My turn! I draw!

00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:28.340
I’ll summon a monster
with high ATK!

00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:31.400
I summon Gagaga Magician!

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:40.520
Gagaga Magician attacks
the face-down defense position monster!

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:43.890
He attacks carelessly.

00:14:43.890 --> 00:14:47.070
Appear, Porcupine Fish!

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:55.140
400 DEF!

00:14:55.140 --> 00:14:57.620
All right! Gagaga Magician wins!

00:14:57.620 --> 00:14:59.250
Its flip effect activates!

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:00.790
Flip effect?

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:07.760
When a Flip Monster is set in face-down defense position,
its flip effect activates when it turns face-up.

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:09.800
The flip effect activates!

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:12.350
You take 400 points of damage!

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:16.930
Not bad!

00:15:17.360 --> 00:15:20.440
But Gagaga has higher ATK!

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:23.360
I win!

00:15:25.910 --> 00:15:27.140
You got me!

00:15:27.140 --> 00:15:29.070
That makes us even!

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:30.980
I end my turn!

00:15:30.980 --> 00:15:33.720
Impressive, Yuma!
I can’t take you lightly!

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:38.290
But I took away
Yuma’s LP!

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:40.180
Hooray!

00:15:40.180 --> 00:15:42.000
Tokunosuke...

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:45.500
He uses Flip Monsters.

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:47.000
Thanks for your time.

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:53.980
Taichi’s mother said
that he went to school as usual.

00:15:53.980 --> 00:15:56.380
Yeah. What’s going on?

00:15:57.020 --> 00:16:00.380
Maybe there’s
a hint in the photos.

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:02.740
That’s right! The photos!

00:16:02.740 --> 00:16:05.160
Maybe we can prove Yuma’s innocence.

00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:08.320
My turn! I draw!

00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:11.070
I set a monster
in defense position!

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:14.380
A face-down defense position monster.

00:16:14.380 --> 00:16:16.490
He’s aiming for another flip effect!

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:19.000
Then I set two cards.

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:20.810
I end my turn!

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:24.260
He’s expecting Yuma to attack.

00:16:24.260 --> 00:16:25.920
What is he aiming for?

00:16:26.320 --> 00:16:27.840
Here I go!

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:29.460
My turn! I draw!

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:31.880
I summon Full Elf!

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:40.020
Full Elf attacks your face-down
defense position monster!

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:42.800
Don’t attack that face-down
defense position monster!

00:16:42.800 --> 00:16:43.830
Be quiet!

00:16:43.830 --> 00:16:51.940
Even if I take flip effect damage, if Full Elf destroys the face-down
defense position monster, Gagaga Magician can attack him directly!

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:53.650
Go, Full Elf!

00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:56.110
Attack his face-down defense position monster!

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:57.870
I knew he’d attack me!

00:16:57.870 --> 00:17:00.090
Appear, Chew Bone!

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:04.710
300 DEF?

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:06.670
I can beat that!

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:08.130
Flip effect!

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:16.180
I can Special Summon up to three Chew Bone Jrs
from my deck onto your field in defense position.

00:17:19.690 --> 00:17:21.810
Summon onto my field?

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:31.730
Hooray! I successfully Special Summoned!

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:37.530
Tokunosuke, it’s pointless
to summon monsters onto my field.

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:41.520
Oh no! I misunderstood the effect!

00:17:41.520 --> 00:17:42.870
Misunderstood?

00:17:44.650 --> 00:17:46.490
I do that a lot too.

00:17:46.490 --> 00:17:47.830
I understand how you feel!

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:49.790
But a duel is a duel.

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:50.800
I won’t show any mercy.

00:17:52.740 --> 00:17:56.510
Gagaga Magician attacks you directly!

00:18:01.840 --> 00:18:05.560
All right! 3600 vs. 2500 LP!

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:07.700
I turned the tables! Now I’ll—

00:18:07.700 --> 00:18:09.610
Wait a second!

00:18:10.370 --> 00:18:12.860
You’re not going to Xyz Summon?

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:14.360
Xyz Summon?

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:16.960
That idiot doesn’t realize it!

00:18:16.960 --> 00:18:20.480
Yuma, you don’t have to be nice
because I made a mistake.

00:18:22.260 --> 00:18:26.880
The mistake I made
by summoning Level 1 Chew Bone Jrs!

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:30.390
There are three Level 1 monsters!

00:18:30.390 --> 00:18:33.440
I see! I can Xyz Summon!

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:35.010
He’s a handful.

00:18:35.010 --> 00:18:39.010
He’s leading Yuma to Xyz Summon.

00:18:40.900 --> 00:18:42.180
Is it that card?

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:46.140
I overlay three
Level 1 Chew Bone Jrs!

00:18:46.140 --> 00:18:46.850
It’s a trap!

00:18:48.450 --> 00:18:51.690
With these three monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:53.360
Xyz Summon!

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:56.310
Appear, Baby Tiragon!

00:19:15.230 --> 00:19:18.910
I did it! I successfully
Xyz Summoned!

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:24.470
You fell for it, Yuma Tsukumo!

00:19:25.340 --> 00:19:26.720
Fell for it?

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:29.690
This card is
the Continuous Trap Ultra C.

00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:31.150
Ultra C?

00:19:31.150 --> 00:19:35.400
With Ultra C, when Baby Tiragon
is summoned onto your field...

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:44.010
I can Special Summon one Xyz Monster in your Extra
Deck onto my field and equip it with this card.

00:19:44.010 --> 00:19:46.290
From my Extra Deck?

00:19:46.290 --> 00:19:50.000
In other words, Utopia is mine!

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:51.710
This match is mine!

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:56.210
Xyz Summoning Baby
Tiragon ended your luck!

00:19:57.030 --> 00:20:04.180
In order to make you Xyz Summon Baby Tiragon,
he Special Summoned Chew Bone Jrs onto your field.

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:05.890
No way!

00:20:06.910 --> 00:20:11.520
But how did Tokunosuke know
that I had Baby Tiragon?

00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:16.980
I saved my
allowance to buy it.

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:22.940
Tokunosuke, you sent the fan mail!

00:20:23.410 --> 00:20:25.720
That’s not all.

00:20:25.720 --> 00:20:32.080
I also sent fake photos to everyone’s cell phones so that
you’d be all alone, and I could get close to you!

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:33.330
You?

00:20:33.330 --> 00:20:35.730
There’s always something behind everything.

00:20:35.730 --> 00:20:38.900
Such as a fool
receiving a fan letter.

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:41.800
Or fake photos being sent
to everyone’s cell phones.

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:44.080
And also this duel!

00:20:44.080 --> 00:20:46.760
Look at the piece
of paper on your back!

00:20:46.760 --> 00:20:48.170
Paper on my back?

00:20:49.250 --> 00:20:51.210
When was this stuck on me?

00:20:51.210 --> 00:20:58.780
I agree that the winner of this duel gets
to take one card from the loser.

00:20:58.780 --> 00:21:00.650
Ante rule.

00:21:01.520 --> 00:21:03.110
Tokunosuke!

00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:06.380
If I win, I’ll take Utopia!

00:21:06.380 --> 00:21:07.580
The Number?

00:21:07.580 --> 00:21:10.580
You were tricking me
from the start!

00:21:11.590 --> 00:21:17.340
You lied when you said
that you believed and supported me!

00:21:17.340 --> 00:21:19.310
The world is full of behind-the-scenes!

00:21:19.310 --> 00:21:21.050
It’s your fault for being tricked!

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:23.050
Tokunosuke!

00:21:23.050 --> 00:21:24.980
This is what humans hide.

00:21:24.980 --> 00:21:28.010
This is his strange power.

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:29.940
Prepare yourself!

00:21:29.940 --> 00:21:34.190
I activate
the Continuous Trap Ultra C!

00:21:36.150 --> 00:21:40.860
I Special Summon Utopia
from Yuma’s Extra Deck!

00:21:41.780 --> 00:21:44.700
I equip this card!

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:48.320
Appear, Utopia!

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:04.550
He stole Utopia!

00:22:12.810 --> 00:22:15.040
Let’s start the duel!

00:22:15.040 --> 00:22:16.790
This week’s quiz:

00:22:16.790 --> 00:22:19.780
Gogogo Golem has 1800 ATK.

00:22:19.780 --> 00:22:24.860
What happens when it battles Crashbug Y
with 1400 ATK?

00:22:30.070 --> 00:22:34.700
Today’s test is hard
Can’t avoid pleasure and temptation

00:22:34.700 --> 00:22:39.560
I want to go home and watch TV
Recent cartoons are entertaining

00:22:49.840 --> 00:22:54.300
Anyway, tests are hard
Language, math and English are especially hard

00:22:54.300 --> 00:22:59.520
Average scores in science and social studies
I’m only good at P.E.

00:22:59.520 --> 00:23:01.940
(Wait, Baby!) The expected

00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:04.570
(What’s that, Baby!) Answers

00:23:04.570 --> 00:23:07.160
(Wait a sec, Baby!) Remember them

00:23:07.160 --> 00:23:08.860
(What are we!? Baby!) For who

00:23:08.860 --> 00:23:13.460
Let’s say I wrote
the correct answers on that sheet

00:23:13.460 --> 00:23:18.080
Will that change the future a year
or a decade from now?

00:23:18.120 --> 00:23:23.400
The world I drew
at the edge of dreams

00:23:23.400 --> 00:23:28.130
Someday I’ll race in the sky

00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:33.260
Nobody can threaten my heart

00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:36.960
Nothing is correct!

00:23:42.060 --> 00:23:46.940
Tokunosuke, why do you need to win so badly
that you have to trick people?

00:23:46.940 --> 00:23:48.240
That’s what a duel is!

00:23:48.240 --> 00:23:50.190
There’s no point
if I don’t win!

00:23:50.190 --> 00:23:50.740
You’re wrong!

00:23:51.130 --> 00:23:52.490
That’s not what a duel is!

00:23:52.490 --> 00:23:55.540
I’ll take all your Numbers!

00:23:55.540 --> 00:23:58.450
Tetsuo, we’ll prove
that Yuma is innocent!

00:23:58.450 --> 00:24:01.500
Protect Baby Tiragon...

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:10.010
Traitorous Numbers?!

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:10.010
\h\hTraitorous Numbers?!\h\h

00:24:02.170 --> 00:24:06.100
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZEXAL:
“Traitorous Numbers?!”

00:24:06.100 --> 00:24:08.640
I’m kattobing!

00:24:11.360 --> 00:24:15.220
Gogogo Golem destroys Crashbug Y!

00:24:15.220 --> 00:24:21.510
And the opponent takes 400 points of damage—
that’s the difference in their ATK!

00:24:21.510 --> 00:24:23.140
You did it!
